  characteristic  the struggle was real and it worked as  he always had makeup on his fingers and  under his fingernails and everything as  he would have from from putting it on  just his hand number 12. she was fit as  a feline anne hathaway was cast as  catwoman and when she was the actress  went straight into the gym and worked  for a full 10 months the suit thoughts  of the suit changing my life so i would  fit into that suit it dominated my year  making sure she would fit into the tiny  costume was just half the battle though  i mean it's not a pair of sweatpants i  wouldn't describe it as that kind of  comfortable actually wearing the  restrictive outfit while filming was a  nightmare and drove hathaway to the  point that she was calling it a  psychological terrorist  you've given them everything  number thirteen  suit up or sew up michelle pfeiffer's  catwoman costume or as pfeiffer called  it the most uncomfortable thing i've  ever worn was so tight that she was  literally sewn into it pfeiffer would  get coated in powder to slip herself in  smoothly and then got vacuum sealed into  the suit for real it was probably really  unhealthy and it would literally just  start to squeeze my skin she struggled  as much as batman did when it came to  getting out of the suit to go to the  washroom always needing help to take a  bathroom break  i thought i can't walk  i can't breathe i can't hear eventually  the costume designer made some  adjustments so the actress could  actually get to the washroom more easily  but performing the action wasn't any  simpler  i can't act  fortunately production gave her a bit of  a break and she was only allowed to wear  the suit for a few hours at a time  number fourteen  it looks cool but it doesn't feel so  cool two of the og batmans michael  keaton and george clooney had to suffer  through two of the stiffest batman suits  in history filming was a brutal  experience because of how much action  they were actually playing out leaving  both performers extremely sore day after  day while both had stiff suits keaton's  was the worst one yet he still brought  an epic performance  number 15  superhero costumes were tough in the 90s  velkilmer suited up but it required a  bit of time getting out of it at the end  of a shoot that would be another 45  minutes needed to go to the bathroom  helpers were always required to make  that happen on top of it all the actor  could hardly hear with the heavy and  claustrophobic mask on  how he managed to so convincingly play a  superhero under these stressful  conditions really is a mystery  in gotham city looking this cool is  painful it's a cross every actor has to  bear but some got off easier than others  which batman costume did you like most

